{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The test leads fit my breadboards, jumper wires, and electronic components because they would help me make temporary connections while testing a circuit.",
    "The clips offer a practical addition to the small electronics supplies I have bought, with a clear use alongside those items."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The 12V relay harnesses do not follow naturally from my 5V relay module; a similar name does not mean they suit the same circuit.",
    "The attenuator, vacuum pump, and temperature controller require specific equipment or projects that my purchases do not establish.",
    "The washers, exterior screws, epoxy, and lifting pulley would need a particular repair or building task to be useful to me now, and the children's masks have no apparent connection to my needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My occasional purchases of hardware and tools seem to have been treated as a continuing need for many kinds of workshop supplies.",
    "My thermometer and caster purchases seem to have been stretched into needs for temperature automation and heavy lifting, even though those are different tasks."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The strongest connection across my electronics purchases is small circuit assembly and testing, where compatible connection supplies have an obvious purpose.",
    "Voltage, equipment requirements, and the exact task matter to me more than a shared word such as relay or temperature.",
    "My purchases are spread over years, so an older project purchase alone gives little reason to assume I need a specialized accessory now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The test leads understood my circuit-building interests, but most other choices assumed specific current projects from loosely related past purchases."
}"}
